WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.050
Speaker 1: Let's keep talking a little bit
about foreign policy.

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:06.240
One other Joe Biden foreign policy note.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.809
Joe Biden did have a call, phone call with
Russian President Vladimir Putin.

00:00:10.809 --> 00:00:15.129
And I'm going to say this in a particular
way, but I'm not necessarily attaching value

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:16.460
judgment to it.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:21.231
Joe Biden stood up to Vladimir Putin during
this phone call in a way that Donald Trump

00:00:21.231 --> 00:00:22.231
never did.

00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:26.070
Now, that doesn't mean we're cheering for
Joe Biden to go to war with Russia.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:31.480
We're not this doesn't mean we are cheering
for Joe Biden to be unnecessarily hostile

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.910
or adversarial with Vladimir Putin.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:39.660
This is it almost shouldn't even be a big
deal that this is how Joe Biden managed the

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.610
phone call with Vladimir Putin.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.780
It's just not the way Donald Trump operated.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:50.800
Donald Trump was enamored by and deferred
to various authoritarian leaders around the

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:51.800
world.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.040
We now have a readout from the White House
and we will look at it together.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.930
This was released yesterday.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:01.610
It reads, President Joseph R. Biden Jr. spoke
today with President Vladimir Putin of Russia.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.540
They discussed a number of regional and global
issues, including the intent of the United

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:12.070
States and Russia to pursue a strategic stability
dialog on a range of armed arms control and

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:18.050
emerging security issues, building on the
extension of the new START treaty.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:23.020
President Biden also made clear that the United
States will act firmly in defense of its natural

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.950
natural national interests in response to
Russia's actions, such as cyber intrusions

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:33.890
and election interference, specifically referring
to the cyber intrusions that we know Russia

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:38.090
was involved in recently and the election
interference that we know Russia attempted

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.090
recently.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:44.729
The readout goes on to say President Biden
emphasized the United States unwavering commitment

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:49.040
to Ukraine's sovereignty and territorial integrity.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.479
The president voiced our concerns over the
sudden Russian military buildup in occupied

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:59.270
Crimea on Ukraine's borders and called on
Russia to deescalate tensions.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:04.000
President Biden reaffirmed his goal of building
a stable and predictable relationship with

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:09.539
Russia consistent with U.S. interests, and
proposed a summit meeting in a third country

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:11.450
in the coming months.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:17.050
This is you know, it's not a big deal in that
this is how most presidents deal with other

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:22.580
adversaries who we know have geopolitical
ambitions that may be out of conflict with

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.270
those of the United States.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.930
It's not about picking a side.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:30.800
It's we have countries, nation states exist.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.930
We have multinational collaboration.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.120
We have treaties, we have agreements.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.680
And we expect our leaders to look out for
the best interests of our country.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.680
That's it.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.750
And that's already more than Donald Trump
ever did.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.170
Biden released the content of the call.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.170
Nobody ate the notes.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:56.760
I mean, remember what I'm talking about, that
there was the story of Omarosa, who said that

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:03.390
she walked in on Donald Trump eating paper
after a meeting with Michael Cohen in what

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.530
she believed was an effort to destroy sensitive
information.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.910
OK, that's the reference with eating paper.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.570
Unlike the previous administration, the fact
that we have this readout also means that

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:20.200
the entire transcript of this call is available
to intelligence members that have the appropriate

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:25.470
clearance and access as opposed to never being
created, as was the case with some of Donald

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:28.040
Trump's conversations with Vladimir Putin.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.489
So everything is being managed in a completely
different way.

00:03:31.489 --> 00:03:33.690
It's not about we want war with Russia.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.209
It's not about militarism.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:41.489
We just want a president that's firm and isn't
obviously railroaded by every authoritarian

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:44.520
autocrat that he talks to and seems taken
with.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:50.850
Remember Trump displeased with Angela Merkel,
displeased with for a period of time.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:53.599
Theresa May displeased with Justin.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:04:02.409
Doe and Emmanuel Macron are traditional allies,
but taken by Putin's shows of strength, impressed

00:04:02.409 --> 00:04:06.269
by Kim Jong un.

00:04:06.269 --> 00:04:07.930
It was very, very backwards.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.490
And so this is without war.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:11.780
Nobody's rallying for war.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:19.279
You know, there's going to be some on the
revolutionary left who will say that a commentary

00:04:19.279 --> 00:04:25.529
like mine is beating drums of war against
Russia or arguing for a hostility.

00:04:25.529 --> 00:04:27.009
We're not doing any of those things.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:34.219
It's simply a president who is able to be
cordial but firm in a phone call with another

00:04:34.219 --> 00:04:35.219
world leader.

00:04:35.219 --> 00:04:41.300
It's a president who's not so impressed with
himself that he's even having the conversation

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.990
and is just able to be railroaded and bamboozled
by anyone.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:49.340
It's just a president who understands geopolitics
and understands how you deal with these situations.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:55.249
So I think there's a lot of good signs here
of Joe Biden in the last 24 hours, firm with

00:04:55.249 --> 00:04:59.479
Putin in a phone call saying, we are getting
out of Afghanistan.

00:04:59.479 --> 00:05:04.219
There is a date certain we're getting out
on September 11th, 20 21.

00:05:04.219 --> 00:05:09.139
These are good signs geopolitically in terms
of foreign policy from Joe Biden.

00:05:09.139 --> 00:05:12.360
Doesn't mean he's going to do everything right,
doesn't mean we'll agree with everything he

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.360
does.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:19.219
But certainly much of the fear mongering from
from the right and some on the left as well

00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:24.349
about Joe Biden's going to invade everybody
and expand our presence.

00:05:24.349 --> 00:05:27.120
And it does not seem to be what he's doing
for the time being.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:28.120
And that's a good thing.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.180
I'm glad to see that.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.180
Let me know your thoughts.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:31.810
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman

